WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:01.734
Use this slide to test whether you

00:00:01.747 --> 00:00:03.932
can explain the design decisions rather than

00:00:03.958 --> 00:00:07.929
only recognize the syntax Why keep a

00:00:07.942 --> 00:00:10.653
natural identifier unique even when a surrogate

00:00:10.666 --> 00:00:15.054
primary key exists Why does a many-to-many

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:19.503
relationship need a junction table Which business

00:00:19.517 --> 00:00:21.767
rules belong in CHECK FOREIGN KEY or

00:00:21.793 --> 00:00:26.112
UNIQUE constraints What kind of dependency does

00:00:26.138 --> 00:00:29.509
Second Normal Form address What does Third

00:00:29.522 --> 00:00:33.583
Normal Form remove Why might child line

00:00:33.609 --> 00:00:35.767
items cascade with a parent while master

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.351
data is restricted And why can a

00:00:39.365 --> 00:00:41.957
normalized operational source still feed a star

00:00:41.983 --> 00:00:45.663
schema Try answering each in your own

00:00:45.676 --> 00:00:48.455
words If you can explain the reason

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:51.389
behind the design the SQL implementation becomes

00:00:51.415 --> 00:00:53.323
much easier to remember and adapt
